    "Arp walks upwards through chord degrees of your scale instead of travelling across the field. Density sets how many cells sound, Rhythm how they sit, Band the register. Traverse is the bar the rhythm counts in — on Sparse and Syncopated it also moves which cells sound, and on all six it sets where the accents fall." : {
      "comment" : "Panel text (E4-7, 2026-09-30): SwiftUI literal keys of EchoelStudioView, the instrument — localised by content, no Sources change.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Arp walks upwards through chord degrees of your scale instead of travelling across the field. Density sets how many cells sound, Rhythm how they sit, Band the register. Traverse is the bar the rhythm counts in — on Sparse and Syncopated it also moves which cells sound, and on all six it sets where the accents fall."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Band drift only changes the arp when it crosses into the next register — under about 0.35 it does nothing." : {
      "comment" : "Panel text (E4-7, 2026-09-30): SwiftUI literal keys of EchoelStudioView, the instrument — localised by content, no Sources change.",
