            "value" : "Arp rhythm"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Note length is a fraction of one cell, scaled by the rhythm — Driving stays short even at 1. Below the instrument's 15 ms minimum nothing gets shorter, and the faster the tempo the sooner that floor is reached; a single note never rings longer than one second. A high Laid back also shortens the longest notes: one that starts late cannot fill its cell as well." : {
      "comment" : "Panel text (E4-7, 2026-09-30): SwiftUI literal keys of EchoelStudioView, the instrument — localised by content, no Sources change.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Note length is a fraction of one cell, scaled by the rhythm — Driving stays short even at 1. Below the instrument's 15 ms minimum nothing gets shorter, and the faster the tempo the sooner that floor is reached; a single note never rings longer than one second. A high Laid back also shortens the longest notes: one that starts late cannot fill its cell as well."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "How far behind its own step a note lands, as a fraction of one step — 0 is dead on the grid. The rhythm adds its own on top (Syncopated leans back on the off-beats, Flowing everywhere), and the total can never push a note into the next step. Earlier-than-the-grid is not offered: the instrument can hold a note back, not see one coming." : {
      "comment" : "Panel text (E4-7, 2026-09-30): SwiftUI literal keys of EchoelStudioView, the instrument — localised by content, no Sources change.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "How far behind its own step a note lands, as a fraction of one step — 0 is dead on the grid. The rhythm adds its own on top (Syncopated leans back on the off-beats, Flowing everywhere), and the total can never push a note into the next step. Earlier-than-the-grid is not offered: the instrument can hold a note back, not see one coming."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Sync pulls your touches onto the beat while the transport runs — early ones wait for the grid, late ones get a quiet echo on it. Life sets how much the corrected notes breathe. On swung genres the grid it aims at is the straight one." : {
      "comment" : "Panel text (E4-7, 2026-09-30): SwiftUI literal keys of EchoelStudioView, the instrument — localised by content, no Sources change.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
