    "Safety & Scope" : {
      "comment" : "Learn / guide cards, the six Learn headings and the bio disclaimer (E4-23, 2026-09-30).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Safety & Scope"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For music and self-observation only — not a medical device and not for diagnosis. Readings are approximate; don’t use them for health decisions." : {
      "comment" : "Learn / guide cards, the six Learn headings and the bio disclaimer (E4-23, 2026-09-30).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "For music and self-observation only — not a medical device and not for diagnosis. Readings are approximate; don’t use them for health decisions."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Your first three minutes" : {
      "comment" : "Learn / guide cards, the six Learn headings and the bio disclaimer (E4-23, 2026-09-30).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Your first three minutes"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The app opens on your piece. Here is the way in." : {
      "comment" : "Learn / guide cards, the six Learn headings and the bio disclaimer (E4-23, 2026-09-30).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The app opens on your piece. Here is the way in."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Echoel opens on your piece — the header at the top, five words at the bottom (down the left side when you hold the phone sideways): Arrange, Mixer, Instrument, Browse and Project — with its living picture as a small card over the piece. Arrange shows your tracks and parts and walks you through making one; Mixer sets their levels, Browse holds your sounds and media, Project sets the piece's key and saves, opens and exports. Instrument is where your body plays: press Play at the top and it composes in your key and genre; once it can read your body, your body plays it. Tap the card's resize arrows to make the picture fill the screen; there, the “Studio” chip brings the controls back and the X hides the picture. Nothing sounds until you start it — silence at launch is by design, not a fault." : {
      "comment" : "Learn / guide cards, the six Learn headings and the bio disclaimer (E4-23, 2026-09-30).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Echoel opens on your piece — the header at the top, five words at the bottom (down the left side when you hold the phone sideways): Arrange, Mixer, Instrument, Browse and Project — with its living picture as a small card over the piece. Arrange shows your tracks and parts and walks you through making one; Mixer sets their levels, Browse holds your sounds and media, Project sets the piece's key and saves, opens and exports. Instrument is where your body plays: press Play at the top and it composes in your key and genre; once it can read your body, your body plays it. Tap the card's resize arrows to make the picture fill the screen; there, the “Studio” chip brings the controls back and the X hides the picture. Nothing sounds until you start it — silence at launch is by design, not a fault."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Hear it" : {
      "comment" : "Learn / guide cards, the six Learn headings and the bio disclaimer (E4-23, 2026-09-30).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Hear it"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Press Play; the music is composed, then your body shapes it." : {
      "comment" : "Learn / guide cards, the six Learn headings and the bio disclaimer (E4-23, 2026-09-30).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Press Play; the music is composed, then your body shapes it."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Play starts generated music — harmony, melody and bass in one key, at one tempo, in the genre you chose. Your heart and breath then bend its brightness, its swell and its calm in real time. For your own voice in the loop, switch on “Body voice” in the Bio panel: a held tone that your breath opens and closes — exhale, and it fades; inhale, and it returns. Toning with it, vowels and hums, is a practice of self-observation: you hear your own breathing pattern as sound." : {
      "comment" : "Learn / guide cards, the six Learn headings and the bio disclaimer (E4-23, 2026-09-30).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Play starts generated music — harmony, melody and bass in one key, at one tempo, in the genre you chose. Your heart and breath then bend its brightness, its swell and its calm in real time. For your own voice in the loop, switch on “Body voice” in the Bio panel: a held tone that your breath opens and closes — exhale, and it fades; inhale, and it returns. Toning with it, vowels and hums, is a practice of self-observation: you hear your own breathing pattern as sound."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "See it" : {
      "comment" : "Learn / guide cards, the six Learn headings and the bio disclaimer (E4-23, 2026-09-30).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "See it"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The picture moves with your body — and it is playable." : {
      "comment" : "Learn / guide cards, the six Learn headings and the bio disclaimer (E4-23, 2026-09-30).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The picture moves with your body — and it is playable."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The picture breathes with you: pulse, breath and coherence drive its colour and motion, capped below 3 flashes per second. Touch it to play notes — every touch lands in key, so there is no wrong place. It stays playable at every window size. With Reduce Motion on, the picture stops its motion; the small header monitors keep following the music." : {
      "comment" : "Learn / guide cards, the six Learn headings and the bio disclaimer (E4-23, 2026-09-30).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The picture breathes with you: pulse, breath and coherence drive its colour and motion, capped below 3 flashes per second. Touch it to play notes — every touch lands in key, so there is no wrong place. It stays playable at every window size. With Reduce Motion on, the picture stops its motion; the small header monitors keep following the music."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Feel it" : {
      "comment" : "Learn / guide cards, the six Learn headings and the bio disclaimer (E4-23, 2026-09-30).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Feel it"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The beat in your hand, the bass in your body." : {
      "comment" : "Learn / guide cards, the six Learn headings and the bio disclaimer (E4-23, 2026-09-30).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The beat in your hand, the bass in your body."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Switch on “Haptic beat (feel)” under “Tempo & variations” and the phone pulses on each quarter-note, the downbeat strongest — you can hold time without watching the screen. The sub-bass is tuned to be felt as much as heard: on a sub, in headphones, or through the haptics. Eyes-free by intention: the instrument is playable without looking at it." : {
      "comment" : "Learn / guide cards, the six Learn headings and the bio disclaimer (E4-23, 2026-09-30).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Switch on “Haptic beat (feel)” under “Tempo & variations” and the phone pulses on each quarter-note, the downbeat strongest — you can hold time without watching the screen. The sub-bass is tuned to be felt as much as heard: on a sub, in headphones, or through the haptics. Eyes-free by intention: the instrument is playable without looking at it."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Give it your pulse" : {
      "comment" : "Learn / guide cards, the six Learn headings and the bio disclaimer (E4-23, 2026-09-30).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Give it your pulse"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Start the music first — then a finger on the back camera." : {
      "comment" : "Learn / guide cards, the six Learn headings and the bio disclaimer (E4-23, 2026-09-30).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Start the music first — then a finger on the back camera."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "After you press Play, lay a fingertip flat over the back camera and flash; the torch lights your skin and Echoel reads your heartbeat from it. Hold still and soft — it locks within seconds and tells you when you can let go. A Bluetooth chest strap (Polar and similar) is the most accurate source and frees your hands: choose it from the pulse pill's source menu. An Apple Watch works via Health, a few seconds behind. The order matters: the camera only starts with the music, so a finger before Play reads nothing." : {
      "comment" : "Learn / guide cards, the six Learn headings and the bio disclaimer (E4-23, 2026-09-30).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "After you press Play, lay a fingertip flat over the back camera and flash; the torch lights your skin and Echoel reads your heartbeat from it. Hold still and soft — it locks within seconds and tells you when you can let go. A Bluetooth chest strap (Polar and similar) is the most accurate source and frees your hands: choose it from the pulse pill's source menu. An Apple Watch works via Health, a few seconds behind. The order matters: the camera only starts with the music, so a finger before Play reads nothing."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For every body" : {
      "comment" : "Learn / guide cards, the six Learn headings and the bio disclaimer (E4-23, 2026-09-30).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "For every body"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Hearing, seeing or feeling — any one of them is a way in." : {
      "comment" : "Learn / guide cards, the six Learn headings and the bio disclaimer (E4-23, 2026-09-30).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Hearing, seeing or feeling — any one of them is a way in."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The three channels above are deliberately redundant: the beat can be felt without being seen, the picture read without being heard, the music followed without the screen. VoiceOver speaks the primary controls, text follows your system size, numbers are typed on a large keypad instead of turned on tiny knobs, and Reduce Motion stops the immersive picture's motion without stopping the music. If flashing light affects you, turn Reduce Motion on before you start, and use Blackout in Routing to cut connected fixtures." : {
      "comment" : "Learn / guide cards, the six Learn headings and the bio disclaimer (E4-23, 2026-09-30).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The three channels above are deliberately redundant: the beat can be felt without being seen, the picture read without being heard, the music followed without the screen. VoiceOver speaks the primary controls, text follows your system size, numbers are typed on a large keypad instead of turned on tiny knobs, and Reduce Motion stops the immersive picture's motion without stopping the music. If flashing light affects you, turn Reduce Motion on before you start, and use Blackout in Routing to cut connected fixtures."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When not to use Echoelmusic" : {
      "comment" : "Learn / guide cards, the six Learn headings and the bio disclaimer (E4-23, 2026-09-30).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "When not to use Echoelmusic"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Four limits — read them once, they matter." : {
      "comment" : "Learn / guide cards, the six Learn headings and the bio disclaimer (E4-23, 2026-09-30).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Four limits — read them once, they matter."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Do not use rhythmic audio-visual pacing while driving or operating machinery. Do not use it under the influence of alcohol or drugs. If you are using Echoelmusic alongside any therapeutic programme, coordinate it — and any medication timing — with your own provider; Echoelmusic is not part of a treatment and replaces nothing. Visuals are capped at 3 flashes per second (W3C WCAG). Reduce Motion stops the immersive picture's motion; the small header monitors and any connected lamps keep following the music, rate-limited rather than frozen. If you are photosensitive, turn Reduce Motion on before you start, and use Blackout in Routing to cut connected fixtures. Stop if you feel unwell." : {
      "comment" : "Learn / guide cards, the six Learn headings and the bio disclaimer (E4-23, 2026-09-30).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Do not use rhythmic audio-visual pacing while driving or operating machinery. Do not use it under the influence of alcohol or drugs. If you are using Echoelmusic alongside any therapeutic programme, coordinate it — and any medication timing — with your own provider; Echoelmusic is not part of a treatment and replaces nothing. Visuals are capped at 3 flashes per second (W3C WCAG). Reduce Motion stops the immersive picture's motion; the small header monitors and any connected lamps keep following the music, rate-limited rather than frozen. If you are photosensitive, turn Reduce Motion on before you start, and use Blackout in Routing to cut connected fixtures. Stop if you feel unwell."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Self-observation, not diagnosis" : {
      "comment" : "Learn / guide cards, the six Learn headings and the bio disclaimer (E4-23, 2026-09-30).",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
